/ fast-apps: a new app is made from the actor that calls, taking what's the same for every app made from the same
/ code and making the rest itself. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each stage is a goal, each comment a
/ behaviour we want, and the step under it runs the test that proves it. Tests live under this plan's folder at the
/ path of what they test. The plang here is intent: each test is written so it builds and goes red before its stage,
/ and the coder makes it green. The text is start.md; what tests can't show (the measurements) is there too.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4
- call Stage5

Stage1
/ an app's step cache goes with its app: disposing the app disposes its cache — C# test CacheLifetimeTests
/ (today app/this.cs:174 makes a Memory cache and DisposeAsync never disposes it)
/ a request app leaves nothing behind: 3,000 request apps made and disposed, memory after stays flat — C# test
/ RequestAppsLeaveNothingBehindTests (red today: the step cache's MemoryCache stays)

Stage2
/ (the in-process parent is deferred to its first user, decision 18: a test's %!app.parent% stays false; its test TestAppHasItsRunnerAsParent went to the backlog with it)
/ a child's System is born from the actor that calls: it has the caller's identity — C# test ChildSystemTests
/ (AChildsSystem_HasItsCallersIdentity)
/ a child stops when the actor that made it stops: cancelling the caller cancels the child — C# test ChildSystemTests
/ (AChildsSystem_StopsWithItsCaller)
/ a child's System is its own actor: a variable it sets, a channel it registers and a setting it writes are not the
/ caller's — C# test ChildSystemTests (AChildsSystem_KeepsItsOwnMemoryChannelsAndSettings)
/ the code's facts are read once per code: a sub app reads no class at its birth — C# test CodeFactsTests
/ (AChildsTypeList_HoldsNothingOfItsOwn_AtBirth, AnAppNoActorMade_ReadsItsOwnFacts)

Stage3
/ a sub app keeps its parent's type list whole under a layer of its own: a type in it is the parent's own object —
/ C# test SharedTypeListTests (AChildsType_IsItsParentsType)
/ what a sub app adds is its own alone: neither its parent nor a sibling has it — C# test SharedTypeListTests
/ (ATypeASubAppAdds_IsOnlyItsOwn)
/ a kind added to a type its parent holds is refused, naming the type (TypesShared), until sub apps own their code —
/ C# test SharedTypeListTests (AKindOnAParentsType_IsRefused_NamingIt)
/ the list a sub app is over refuses its own app's additions, saying why — C# test SharedTypeListTests
/ (TheSharedList_RefusesItsOwnAppsAddition)
/ the plugin's type joins only the sub app that loaded it, and its sibling never sees it
- call /plan/fast-apps/app/type/plugin/PluginTypeJoinsOnlyItsApp
- call /plan/fast-apps/app/type/plugin/SiblingDoesNotSeeThePluginType
/ the module registry the same way, refused as ModuleShared — C# test SharedModuleTests
/ a binding made while a program runs is held on the context of the actor that made it: it fires only in its own app
/ and goes with it — C# tests HoldTests, HeldBindingTests
- call /plan/fast-apps/app/event/BindingStaysInItsTest
- call /plan/fast-apps/app/event/SiblingDoesNotSeeTheBinding
/ a run never writes an object its app shares: a type takes no prior into its history — C# test SharedEntryWritesTests
/ a sub app finds the goal its parent read: the same goal object, no second .pr read — C# test SharedGoalTests
/ (AChild_FindsItsParentsGoal); many sub apps loading one goal make one read (ManySubAppsLoadingOneGoal_MakeOneRead)
/ a goal read after a sub app loads code stays its own, never its parent's — C# test SharedGoalTests
/ (AGoalReadAfterTheSubAppLoadsCode_StaysItsOwn)
/ a goal changed on disk is read again on its next use, with no time window — C# test SharedGoalTests
/ (AGoalChangedOnDisk_IsReadAgain)
/ the kind lookup takes no lock: two apps sharing a type look up its kinds at once — C# test KindLookupTests

Stage4
/ a birth makes only what's asked for: a bare app's birth makes no module action, no code provider, no store file —
/ C# test BirthTests (ABareApp_MakesNothingNotAsked)
/ path's schemes are kind classes: file, http and https resolve with nothing added to the type list at birth — C# test
/ PathSchemeTests (TheSchemes_AreKindsOfPath)
/ what's made on first ask is the same as what a birth made before: every module's actions, every setting's default,
/ the system variables — the existing suites are this stage's guard

Stage5
/ a list's positional read takes no lock: list[i] and its count read its snapshot — C# test ListSnapshotReadTests
/ an in-memory store nothing has written answers empty without opening SQLite — C# test EmptyStoreTests
/ (AnUnwrittenStore_AnswersEmpty_WithoutOpening)
/ class facts are read once per code: choice sets, action properties, setting paths and defaults — C# test
/ ClassFactsTests
